Product thinking, AI engineering, and lessons from building developer tools.
Product
Aug 5, 2026
·
5 min read
When twelve users report the same auth bug through different channels, you get twelve Jira tickets, twelve Slack pings, and zero signal. Here's how cosine-similarity deduplication at the embedding level gives you one canonical issue.
Read article →
AI
7 min read
Sentiment scoring is not opinion mining — here's the difference
VADER scores compound sentiment from -1.0 to +1.0. But a -0.6 score on "the API is completely broken" is not the same as -0.6 on "I wish this had dark mode." We explain how DevX layers category and priority context on top of raw sentiment.
Jul 28, 2026
Engineering
10 min read
Building an 8-stage async AI pipeline on Celery without losing your mind
How we chain normalize → embed → dedup → classify → sentiment → priority → route → digest using Celery canvas, handle partial failures gracefully, and keep every stage idempotent.
Jul 14, 2026
Security
4 min read
How we built the Gmail integration with least-privilege access
We only request gmail.readonly, only read messages that match your configured filter, and poll every 120 seconds instead of using Pub/Sub push subscriptions. Here's the full design and why we made each trade-off.
Jun 30, 2026
Product
6 min read
Routing feedback to the right team without turning it into a full-time job
Configurable routing rules mean a priority >80 bug goes straight to a GitHub issue, while a positive feature request goes to Slack. We walk through the routing agent design and how to set up rules that scale.
Jun 18, 2026
Engineering
8 min read
Tenant isolation in a SaaS PostgreSQL schema — the DevX approach
Every table has a tenant_id. Every query is filtered by it through a global SQLAlchemy event listener. Here's how we ensure one customer can never see another's data, even in the event of a bug.
Jun 4, 2026
