Last updated: August 9, 2026
This Privacy Policy explains how DevX ("DevX", "we", "us", or "our") collects, uses, and shares information when you use our developer feedback platform, including our website, dashboard, feedback widget, and integrations (collectively, the "Service").
Account information.
When you register, we collect your name, email address, password (stored as a salted hash — we never store or have access to your plaintext password), and organization (tenant) details.
Feedback content.
DevX helps you collect and triage feedback from sources you control. Depending on what you connect, this may include content submitted directly through our embeddable web widget, or content you choose to import from third-party tools you authorize us to access, such as GitHub issues, GitLab issues, Slack messages, Discord messages, Jira issues, ClickUp tasks, and Gmail messages (see Section 2 below for Gmail specifically).
Usage and log data.
We keep audit logs of account actions (e.g. status changes to a feedback item) that record the actor, action, timestamp, and originating IP address, for security and accountability purposes.
If you choose to connect a Gmail inbox, DevX requests read-only access (
gmail.readonly
) via Google's OAuth consent flow. We use this access strictly to:
Periodically search the connected inbox using the label(s) and/or search query you configure in DevX (for example, a "feedback" label);
Read the subject line, sender, and body of messages that match that search, and nothing else in the inbox;
Convert each matching message into a feedback record in your DevX account, so it can be triaged alongside feedback from your other connected sources.
We do not read, store, or process any Gmail message that does not match your configured filter. We do not use Gmail data to serve advertisements, and we do not sell Gmail data or any data derived from it to any third party. Access to stored Gmail content is limited to DevX personnel and systems that need it to operate the Service, investigate abuse, or comply with law.
DevX's use and transfer of information received from Google APIs adheres to the
Google API Services User Data Policy
, including the Limited Use requirements.
You can revoke DevX's access to your Gmail account at any time, either from DevX's Integrations settings ("Disconnect") or directly from your
Google Account permissions
. Disconnecting deletes the stored access and refresh tokens for that integration; feedback items already imported are retained as part of your feedback history unless you delete them.
To operate, maintain, and improve the Service — including normalizing, categorizing, scoring the sentiment and priority of, and routing feedback items you've chosen to ingest.
To authenticate you and secure your account.
To send you service-related emails (e.g. password resets, notifications that a feedback item you submitted was resolved).
To generate periodic digests summarizing feedback trends for your organization.
To respond to support requests and enforce our Terms of Service.
We do not sell your personal information or your feedback content. We share information only with:
Infrastructure providers
that host our application, database, and background job processing (including task queue, cache, and object storage services).
AI and machine learning providers
used to process feedback on your behalf — specifically:
NVIDIA NIM
(primary classification and priority scoring via Llama 3.1),
Google Gemini API
(fallback classification, priority scoring, and weekly digest generation), and
HuggingFace Inference API
(semantic embedding). Sentiment analysis is performed locally using VADER and does not involve any third-party API call. We strip common PII patterns (email addresses, phone numbers) from feedback text before it is sent to any external AI provider.
Email delivery providers
, to send transactional emails (e.g. password resets, team invitations) on our behalf.
The third-party tools you connect
(e.g. creating a GitHub issue or posting to a Slack channel), strictly according to the routing rules you configure. No data is sent to a connected tool unless the feedback item meets the routing threshold you set.
Law enforcement or regulators, where required by applicable law.
DevX allows you to generate API keys to authenticate programmatic access to the Service. API keys are stored as one-way hashes (bcrypt, cost factor ≥ 12) — we never store the plaintext key and cannot recover it after generation. You are responsible for keeping your API keys confidential. You can revoke any key at any time from your account settings. Revocation takes effect immediately.
We retain account and feedback data for as long as your account is active, or as needed to provide the Service. Audit logs are retained for up to seven years for security and accountability purposes. You may delete individual feedback items, disconnect any integration, or request full account deletion by contacting us at the email below — we will delete or anonymize your data within a reasonable time, except where retention is required by law.
We use industry-standard measures to protect your data, including encrypted connections (TLS) in transit, bcrypt-hashed password and API key storage (cost factor ≥ 12), per-tenant data isolation at the database level, and rate limiting to help prevent abuse. All mutations are recorded in an append-only audit log. No system is perfectly secure, and we encourage you to use a strong, unique password and to review your connected integrations periodically.
Depending on your location, you may have rights to access, correct, export, or delete your personal information, or to object to certain processing. You can exercise most of these directly in your account settings (e.g. disconnecting an integration, deleting a feedback item) or by contacting us.
If you are located in Nigeria, we process personal data in accordance with the Nigeria Data Protection Act 2023 and the Nigeria Data Protection Regulation ("NDPR"). This includes your rights to be informed of the processing of your personal data, to access the personal data we hold about you, to request correction or deletion of it, and to lodge a complaint with the Nigeria Data Protection Commission ("NDPC") if you believe your rights have been violated.
We use a small number of essential cookies and localStorage values to keep you signed in and protect against cross-site request forgery. We do not use third-party advertising or tracking cookies. For a full breakdown of the cookies we set, see our
Cookie Policy
.
The Service is intended for business use and is not directed to individuals under 16. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children.
Your information may be processed in countries other than your own, including outside Nigeria, because our AI processing and infrastructure partners operate globally. Where we transfer personal data of individuals in Nigeria outside the country, we do so in accordance with the cross-border transfer requirements of the Nigeria Data Protection Act 2023 / NDPR — for example, by confirming the receiving country has an adequate level of data protection, or by putting other legally recognized safeguards in place.
We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. We will update the "Last updated" date above, and for material changes, we will provide additional notice (such as an email) where appropriate.
Questions about this Privacy Policy or your data? Contact us at
support@devx.today
.
© 2026 DevX. Built for excellence.
