These Terms of Service ("Terms") govern your access to and use of DevX's developer feedback platform, including our website, dashboard, feedback widget, and integrations (collectively, the "Service"), operated by DevX Inc. ("DevX", "we", "us", or "our"). By creating an account or otherwise using the Service, you agree to these Terms.
DevX is a developer feedback platform that helps product teams collect, triage, prioritize, and act on feedback from multiple sources. The core Service includes:
An AI-powered ingestion pipeline that normalizes, embeds, deduplicates, classifies, scores the sentiment and priority of, and routes feedback items.
Integrations with GitHub, GitLab, Slack, Jira, and Gmail that let you pull feedback from those sources into DevX automatically.
An embeddable web widget for collecting in-product feedback directly from your users.
Analytics, weekly AI-generated digest reports, and configurable routing rules.
Additional integrations (including Linear and Discord) are in development. Connecting a third-party source requires you to grant DevX the permissions described during each integration\'s authorization flow.
You must provide accurate information when creating an account and are responsible for safeguarding your credentials and for all activity under your account. You must be authorized to act on behalf of your organization if you register on its behalf.
Certain plans include a free trial period. At the end of a trial or billing period, we will not delete your data — access to ingestion, AI processing, routing, and reporting features may be paused until you upgrade or the next billing cycle begins, unless we notify you otherwise. Your existing feedback records remain accessible in a read-only state during any paused period. Fees, where applicable, are described at the point of purchase and are non-refundable except as required by law or as we expressly state.
You (or your organization) retain ownership of the feedback content you submit or import through the Service ("Your Content"). You grant DevX a worldwide, non-exclusive license to host, store, process, transmit, and display Your Content solely to provide and improve the Service for you — including automated classification, sentiment scoring, prioritization, deduplication, and routing to destinations you configure.
You represent that you have the necessary rights and permissions to submit or authorize the import of Your Content, including any content sourced from a connected Gmail inbox, Slack workspace, or other third-party account.
Connecting a third-party account (e.g. Google, GitHub, Slack, Jira, Discord, ClickUp) is optional and governed by that provider's own terms and privacy policy, in addition to these Terms. DevX is not responsible for the availability, accuracy, or conduct of third-party services. You may disconnect any integration at any time from your account settings.
You agree not to:
Use the Service to store or transmit unlawful, infringing, or malicious content.
Attempt to gain unauthorized access to the Service, other accounts, or connected integrations.
Reverse engineer, scrape, or resell the Service without our written permission.
Use the Service in a way that violates the terms of any connected third-party platform.
DevX and its licensors retain all rights, title, and interest in the Service itself (excluding Your Content), including our software, branding, and documentation.
THE SERVICE IS PROVIDED "AS IS" WITHOUT WARRANTIES OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE, AND NON-INFRINGEMENT. THE AI PIPELINE USES THIRD-PARTY MODELS (INCLUDING NVIDIA NIM, GOOGLE GEMINI, AND HUGGINGFACE MODELS) THAT MAY PRODUCE INCORRECT, INCOMPLETE, OR INCONSISTENT OUTPUTS. WE DO NOT WARRANT THAT AUTOMATED CLASSIFICATION, SENTIMENT SCORING, PRIORITY SCORING, OR DIGEST SUMMARIES WILL BE ACCURATE, COMPLETE, OR ERROR-FREE. YOU SHOULD INDEPENDENTLY VERIFY ANY AI-GENERATED OUTPUT BEFORE ACTING ON IT.
TO THE MAXIMUM EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW, DEVX WILL NOT BE LIABLE FOR ANY INDIRECT, INCIDENTAL, SPECIAL, CONSEQUENTIAL, OR PUNITIVE DAMAGES, OR ANY LOSS OF PROFITS, DATA, OR GOODWILL, ARISING FROM YOUR USE OF THE SERVICE.
You may stop using the Service and delete your account at any time. We may suspend or terminate your access if you materially breach these Terms and do not cure the breach after notice, or immediately if necessary to protect the Service or other users.
We may update these Terms from time to time. We will update the "Last updated" date above and, for material changes, provide additional notice where appropriate. Continued use of the Service after changes take effect constitutes acceptance of the revised Terms.
These Terms are governed by the laws of the Federal Republic of Nigeria, without regard to its conflict-of-laws principles, and any dispute arising out of or relating to these Terms or the Service shall be subject to the exclusive jurisdiction of the courts of Nigeria.
