Cookies
Log In
Last updated: August 9, 2026
This Cookie Policy explains what cookies and similar storage mechanisms DevX uses, why we use them, and how you can control them. By using the Service, you consent to our use of the cookies described in this policy.
Cookies are small text files that a website stores on your browser when you visit. They allow the site to remember information between page loads and sessions. We also use browser
localStorage
for certain authentication tokens where cookie-based delivery is restricted by browser security policies (e.g. cross-origin deployments).
DevX sets only
essential
cookies. We do not set advertising, analytics tracking, or third-party cookies of any kind.
access_token
Type
HttpOnly, Secure cookie (primary) · localStorage (fallback for cross-origin)
Lifetime
15 minutes (JWT expiry)
Purpose
Authenticates your session with the DevX API. Contains a signed JWT that identifies your account and tenant. The HttpOnly flag prevents JavaScript from reading it, reducing XSS exposure.
Essential?
Yes — the Service cannot function without it.
refresh_token
Type
HttpOnly, Secure cookie
Lifetime
7 days
Purpose
Used to silently obtain a new access token when yours expires, so you stay logged in without re-entering your password. Sent only to the token refresh endpoint (
/v1/auth/refresh
), not on every API request.
Essential?
Yes — required to maintain a persistent login session.
csrf_token
Type
JavaScript-readable cookie (double-submit CSRF pattern)
Lifetime
Session (cleared when browser tab is closed)
Purpose
Protects against Cross-Site Request Forgery (CSRF) attacks. The frontend reads this value and echoes it back in an
X-CSRF-Token
request header; our API verifies the two values match before processing any state-changing request.
Essential?
Yes — required for secure form submissions and API mutations.
In environments where cross-origin cookie delivery is blocked by browser third-party cookie restrictions (e.g. when the frontend and backend are on different domains), DevX falls back to storing the access token in
localStorage
and sending it as a
Bearer
token in the
Authorization
header. This data is:
Scoped to the DevX origin and not accessible to other sites.
Cleared when you log out.
Not shared with any third party.
DevX does
not
use any third-party cookies for advertising, behavioural tracking, or analytics. We do not embed third-party scripts (such as Google Analytics, Meta Pixel, or ad networks) that would set cookies on your behalf. OAuth provider cookies (set by Google, GitHub, Slack, etc. during their own authorization flows) are outside our control and governed by those providers' own cookie policies.
Because all cookies DevX sets are strictly essential to the operation of the Service, blocking them will prevent the Service from working correctly. You can manage cookies through your browser settings:
Chrome:
Settings → Privacy and Security → Cookies and other site data
Firefox:
Settings → Privacy & Security → Cookies and Site Data
Safari:
Preferences → Privacy → Manage Website Data
Edge:
Settings → Cookies and site permissions → Cookies and site data
You can also clear all DevX-related cookies and localStorage at any time by logging out, which triggers a server-side token revocation and clears all client-side session data.
We may update this Cookie Policy if we add or change the cookies we use. We will update the "Last updated" date above and, for material changes, provide additional notice where appropriate.
Questions about cookies or how we handle your data? Contact us at
support@devx.today
or read our full
Privacy Policy
.
